        "id": 1074459
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T22:12:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Please refer to the description here from Samsung on the requirement for this feature: https://b.corp.google.com/issues/321314635#comment17.\n\n```\nThe 3rd party app should also be able to check whether it is supported or not.\n```\n\nWe have existing feature flags for devices that support nfc card emulation using physical sim card - `FEATURE_NFC_OFF_HOST_CARD_EMULATION_UICC`. This is used by 3p apps to figure out if they can use NFC card emulation on a particular offhost type.",
      "parentUuid": "d8465060_b0771845",
      "revId": "4ff267e9f4c086f861b8997fe908a770291a9210",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1de2319f_e67bd019",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1061144
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-28T23:33:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`hasSystemFeature` should be used when app distributors need to make sure that features of the device that an app may require are available before installing such an app. It is not a runtime check 3rd party apps should be using.\n\nIf a 3rd party app needs to be able to check whether an NFC capability exists at runtime, it should have a dedicated java API for doing so, not a feature returned by `hasSystemFeature`.\n\nThis does not seem an appropriate use of `hasSystemFeature`, regardless of whether previous misuse was approved. Please find a more appropriate place for this capability to be checked (an API on NfcManager or NfcAdapter?). Since this appears to be targeting V, consider temporarily defining a resource config or system property that can eventually be replaced by proper API.",
      "parentUuid": "bb44e7e0_c8262216",
      "revId": "4ff267e9f4c086f861b8997fe908a770291a9210",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
